   A disposable Rust environment. Nothing is saved when it stops.

 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Toolchains   stable 1.98.1 (default), beta, nightly
   Targets      x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, musl (static)
   Editor       IDE tab, rust-analyzer, clippy on save, lldb
   Docs         doc.rust tab, or run cargo doc --open
 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

   START
     cargo new hello             Create a project
     cargo run                   Compile and run
     cargo check                 Type check without linking

   TEST AND LINT
     cargo test                  Run the test suite
     cargo test -- --nocapture   Show println! output
     cargo nextest run           Faster, cleaner test runner
     cargo clippy                Lint with suggestions
     cargo fmt                   Format every file

   WATCH
     bacon                       Live check on every save
     bacon clippy                Live lint on every save
     bacon test                  Live tests on every save

   DEPENDENCIES
     cargo add <crate>           Add a dependency
     cargo update                Update the lockfile
     cargo tree                  Show the dependency graph
     cargo audit                 Scan for known vulnerabilities
     cargo binstall <crate>      Install a tool, prebuilt

   INSPECT
     cargo expand                Show code after macros expand

   RELEASE
     cargo build --release       Optimized build
     cargo build --release --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl
                                 Static binary, no libc needed

   TOOLCHAINS
     cargo +nightly run          Run on nightly
     cargo +beta build           Build on beta
     rustup show                 List what is installed

 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   SHORTCUTS
     c  cargo        cb  build     cr  run       ct  test
     cn  nextest     cl  clippy    cf  fmt

     ll  list files  lt  tree      z <dir>  jump to a folder
     bat <file>  view with color   rg <text>  search code
     Ctrl+R  search history        Ctrl+T  pick a file
 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Hit a compiler error? rustc --explain E0382 spells any code out.
